# counting_rooms:
# CSES 1192, Counting Rooms (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1192), in our own
# words: a map of rows of squares, each floor (true) or wall (false), given as
# a Scott list of rows, each a Scott list of booleans; a room is a largest set
# of floor squares joined by steps left, right, up and down over floor; the
# number of rooms. Part of the CSES port's first batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the floor squares are listed with
# their row and column, in reading order; reach steps from_square to_square holds when a walk of at
# most steps over floor leads from from_square to to_square, by its recursion on steps; a room is
# counted at its first square in reading order, the floor square that no
# earlier floor square reaches within floor steps, floor the number of floor squares
# (a shortest walk visits no square twice). Under tabling the reading shares
# reach steps from_square to_square for each steps, from_square and to_square, about floor^3 steps; the replacement the family
# asks for is a flood fill, about the size of the map.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ, application and
# top, with no choice and no parallel outside top. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer (reach consumes steps, each fold a finite
# list): every top it holds (a bit of a literal that no key expects) stands in a
# branch that a Scott boolean discards, and binary_subtract, which writes no top
# (../common/binary_modular), is never asked for less than zero, since the
# program subtracts only what is no larger. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the
# soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of Definition
# 14 (Lean `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V
# is an answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V
# ⊑_O W, while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W
# to λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "pair")
λ pair _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ binary_subtract _ _
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self row_index rows
        . rows nil
        λ row others
        . append
          ( fixpoint
            ( λ along column_index squares
              . squares nil λfloor rest. floor (cons (pair row_index column_index) λ. along (merge_binary_increment column_index) rest) λ. along (merge_binary_increment column_index) rest
            ) binary_zero row
          ) λ. self (merge_binary_increment row_index) others
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ floor_squares
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ first second
    . merge_binary_equality (merge_binary_increment first) second true λ. merge_binary_equality (merge_binary_increment second) first
  )
λ next_to
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ square other_square
    . square
    λ row_index column_index
    . other_square
    λ other_row_index other_column_index
    . merge_binary_equality row_index other_row_index (next_to column_index other_column_index) λ. merge_binary_equality column_index other_column_index (next_to row_index other_row_index) false
  )
λ adjacent
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ square other_square
    . square λrow_index column_index. other_square λother_row_index other_column_index. merge_binary_equality row_index other_row_index (merge_binary_equality column_index other_column_index) false
  )
λ same
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint λself predicate items. items false λhead tail. predicate head true λ. self predicate tail
  )
λ some_member
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ squares
    . fixpoint
    λ self steps from_square to_square
    . same from_square to_square true
    λ
    . steps false (λ_. some_member (λneighbour. adjacent from_square neighbour (self (binary_subtract steps (binary_odd binary_zero) false) neighbour to_square) false) squares) λ_. some_member (λneighbour. adjacent from_square neighbour (self (binary_subtract steps (binary_odd binary_zero) false) neighbour to_square) false) squares
  )
λ reach
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ map
    . ( λ squares
        . ( λ floor
            . fixpoint
              ( λ self before count rest
                . rest count
                λ square others
                . some_member (λearlier_square. reach squares floor earlier_square square) before (self (cons square before) count others) λ. self (cons square before) (merge_binary_increment count) others
              ) nil binary_zero squares
          ) λ. fixpoint (λlength count items. items count λ_ tail. length (merge_binary_increment count) tail) binary_zero squares
      ) λ. floor_squares map
  )
λ counting_rooms
. export counting_rooms
